Description: add a Makefile shim for the debhelper class
 Upstream ships lower-case ./makefile, which GNU make finds happily, but
 the vos_makefile_engine debhelper class resolves an explicit "Makefile"
 in check_buildsystem and in _mkvars ("make -pn -f Makefile", the source
 of NAME for the install step and of APP_MIME_SIG/LOCALES for the
 catalog step). Without this file the compile succeeds and then
 dh_auto_install dies with "Makefile-Engine: NAME is not set" while the
 catalogs are silently skipped. GNU make prefers ./makefile over
 ./Makefile, so the actual build still runs upstream's file; through
 "-f Makefile" the include below yields the same definitions.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/Tipster

--- /dev/null
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Debhelper build-system shim for the V\OS class-1 build.
+#
+# Upstream keeps its makefile in lower-case ./makefile (GNU make finds
+# it fine), but the vos_makefile_engine debhelper class reads and
+# queries an explicit "Makefile" (its check_buildsystem, its _mkvars
+# "make -pn -f Makefile" that yields NAME for the install step and the
+# APP_MIME_SIG/LOCALES for the catalog step). Without this file the
+# build compiles but dh_auto_install dies with "Makefile-Engine: NAME
+# is not set" and the catalogs are silently skipped. GNU make prefers
+# ./makefile over ./Makefile, so the engine build itself still runs
+# upstream's own file untouched; this shim is only ever read through
+# "-f Makefile", where the include below pulls the same definitions in.
+include makefile
